\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of $\\mathbf r'(1)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n‖r^{′}(1)‖ &= \\sqrt{0^{2} + 3^{2} + 4^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{25} \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize $\\mathbf r'(1)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(1,3,2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nT(1) &= (r^{′}(1))/(‖r^{′}(1)‖) \\\\\n&= \\frac{3j + 4k}{5} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{5}j + \\frac{4}{5}k\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535066 false] [17592186119480 1145 "For a curve ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/d7ec57597ee1ec3ed5d675c6d1cfde0115309f037e92d4aae963be1e54c97173.png) the unit tangent vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/beaa6501c934b5c7325c3b3385bae9fcc0388a74d5983995c83f4d8813e93f06.png) at the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/5313a9faaa4dde443c2eb79dedc7d917f6640579d0f038ffaf045ed01fd465f4.png) is given by \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/ff0324d951fb404b12736c08195532ce8d2fe57cae5baf845673b3626b871eb6.png) \n\nFirst, we find the value of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/7a5dc70352bd991ad75358cc62cef8d67afbb5cb00da1578f008a0b392d2385d.png) that corresponds to the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/83fbafba1d5d5be0d132254724f1cadcd31c51dc923c63113d0f393bf6bf94bc.png) on the given curve. We know that\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/aebba9c47fe0ea053b4fc1924e7f3a97ee17dc60fc074091ba0f6c303301cfda.png)\nIn the above equation, the first component in each of the two vectors is equal to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/549c2a20cf7ec79cb4b26e39d950105c670a74452b2d7d024d3d5e64d553ecbe.png) Equating the other two components gives the system\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/187d4f3cd4d27fdac888ccf0d88c58f0cfb073913999f5767584476d9d2d4e10.png)\nFrom the first equation, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/02ad803439ddfa163c4788fb00ff86c65d3e0dc0711af87290695a8f06471e81.png) This value satisfies the second equation too. Therefore, the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/3d4f13f8fb24239874d83180ba75954be6d86ec8bb6e339bea3a0c1c9a4edae4.png) is at the tip of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/7479ebb2b1c8ed8146f6833341d2e732dcd91f86781823d36906dd19cadca82c.png) \n\nNow, we calculate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/2a03e92cf496f1508de5344917e1f5fe5574f9801a0ef229649288a29c15044b.png) and evaluate it at ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/06f646a39990b7ed47b7ab431b54ea320a05650e5e4f6df6f51812460536154b.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/9432511f61bf63030d95771cdc107682a61444fe925dab681ab8388b4a48524e.png) \n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050604/assets/3b10ec5094240cfd7f221bc22e19a29d74b4a69d2788887265041cc7db5291ca.png)\n\n![](/home/jake/Devel