{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,p(t)+{t}^{3}\\,{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =3(1)^{2}\\,p(1)+(1)^{3}\\,{p}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =3(-2\\,i+\\,j+\\,k)+(3\\,i-3\\,j+\\,k) \\\\  & =-6\\,i+3\\,j+3k+3\\,i-3\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =-3\\,i+4\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖r(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(0)^{2}+(4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-3\\,i+4\\,k) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\,i+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=1$ is  $T(1)=-\\frac{3}{5}\\,i+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k.$" 13194139535066 true] [17592186329454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329455 13194139535066 true] [17592186329454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329456 13194139535066 true] [17592186329454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329457 13194139535066 true] [17592186329454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329458 13194139535066 true] [17592186329454 1000 #edb/ref 17592186329459 13194139535066 true] [17592186329454 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535066 true] [17592186329454 1041 "selection" 13194139535066 true] [17592186329454 1104 #edb/ref 17592186329456 13194139535066 true] [17592186329454 1110 #uuid "e5b4f5a3-df25-555a-b870-800afaa4693e" 13194139535066 true] [17592186329455 1034 "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{5}\\,i+\\frac{1}{5}\\,j+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k" 13194139535066 true] [17592186329455 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535066 true] [17592186329455 1111 #uuid "6f865317-1304-5216-b706-d86fdc39ae8e" 13194139535066 true] [17592186329456 1034 "-\\frac{3}{5}\\,i+\\frac{4}{5}\\,k" 13194139535066 true] [17592186329456 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535066 true] [17592186329456 1111 #uuid "0ba54814-9804-5efe-affe-9a1bb275f269" 13194139535066 true] [17592186329457 1034 "-\\frac{3}{5}\\,j+\\frac{2}{5}\\,k" 13194139535066 true] [17592186329457 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 1